# FABLE-SONNET-OCC-ROOT-20260924-146 commit 2 / D-25: orphan, measured and
# completed -- the original never called go(), so a broken address write
# through an own-declared formal would have passed silently. @: n (address
# of an own-declared local formal) into a pointer parameter, write-back read.
# The root speaks the host's exit (`sendMessage: exit`), and `got: go(0U)` stores an int into a
# size_t own through the root's conversion edge (implements-port slice 13); `go` returns its
# size_t n through the return's edge (slice 4).
fn: set_one (@: size_t p) int
    \p: 1U
    return: 0
end: set_one
fn: go (size_t: n) int
    n: 0U
    set_one(@: n)
    return: n
end: go

size_t: got
got: go(0U)
if: got != 1U
    sendMessage: exit(exit_code: 81; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
    return
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: 7; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
